7e62237f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jackela/AI-Recruitment-Clerk/commits/bf7e224d3a7cc904b334f4d21b21dae17e62237f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27112787?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jackela/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jackela/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jackela/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jackela/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jackela","id":27112787,"login":"Jackela","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MTEyNzg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jackela/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jackela/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jackela/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jackela/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jackela/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jackela","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jackela/AI-Recruitment-Clerk/commits/40a1b8845bd73535038fcedc405ef5d328822e33/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-26T04:33:17Z","email":"k740724287@gmail.com","name":"Jackela"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-26T04:33:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: [CLEAN-001] Replace `any` types in 8 shared-dtos files (#47)\n\n* refactor: [CLEAN-001] Replace `any` types in 8 shared-dtos files\n\nPartial progress on CLEAN-001 - fixing `any` type usages in shared-dtos library.\n\nChanges:\n- Replace `Record<string, any>` with `Record<string, unknown>`\n- Replace `data: any` in restore methods with typed interfaces\n- Replace `...args: any[]` with `...args: unknown[]` in decorators\n- Replace `event: any` with `DomainEvent` or `unknown` with type guards\n\nFiles fixed:\n- contracts/analytics.contracts.ts\n- domains/analytics.rules.ts\n- domains/incentive.dto.ts\n- domains/incentive.rules.ts\n- domains/usage-limit.service.ts\n- domains/user-management.dto.ts\n- encryption/encryption.service.ts\n- infrastructure/redis/redis.client.ts\n\nRemaining: 19 files still have `any` usages\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: Fix broken links, standardize versions, add env validation to microservices\n\n- Fix README.md documentation links to point to existing files\n- Update Node.js version requirement from 18+ to 20.18.0+ (matches CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- Fix Angular version badge in Chinese README from 18 to 20\n- Standardize DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md to use npm instead of pnpm\n- Add validateEnv() to all 4 microservices for fail-fast startup:\n  - resume-parser-svc\n  - jd-extractor-svc\n  - scoring-engine-svc\n  - report-generator-svc\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [CLEAN-001] Verify and complete shared-dtos any type removal\n\nVerified CLEAN-001 acceptance criteria are met:\n- No @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any errors in shared-dtos source files\n- npm run lint for shared-dtos passes (0 errors, 21 warnings for different rules)\n- npm test passes (819 tests)\n\nThe previous commit (8d1e061) already fixed most any types. Remaining any\nusages are only in test files (.spec.ts, .test.ts) which are acceptable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [CLEAN-002] Fix any types in app-gateway services\n\n- Create analytics.dto.ts with proper typed DTOs\n- Reorder ReportFiltersDto before GenerateReportDto to fix circular dependency\n- Fix test to provide required DTO properties (metricName, value)\n- All lint checks pass with 0 any type errors\n- All 398 tests pass\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [CLEAN-003] Fix any types in resume-parser-svc\n\n- Created internal types file (parsing.types.ts) with proper type definitions\n- Updated ResumeSubmittedEvent with organizationId and fileMetadata fields\n- Replaced all `any` types in source files with proper typed interfaces:\n  - ResumeSubmittedEventData, ResumeParseSuccessResult, RetryOriginalData\n  - HealthCheckDetails, ResumeStatusUpdateData, SkillsQueryFilter, SortOption\n  - ExperienceMetrics, SecuredResumeDto\n- Fixed type compatibility issues with Mongoose Sort and Record<string, unknown>\n- All 432 tests pass, lint passes with 0 errors\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [CLEAN-004] Fix any types in scoring-engine-svc\n\n- Created internal interfaces for Gemini API response types:\n  - SemanticMatchResponse for skill matching\n  - SkillImprovementSuggestion and ImprovementSuggestionsResponse\n- Used generic type parameter with generateStructuredResponse<T>()\n- All 183 tests pass, lint passes with 0 errors\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [CLEAN-005] Fix any types in frontend\n\n- Replace all `any` types with proper TypeScript types in frontend source files\n- Use `unknown` with type guards for error handling\n- Make SwipeEvent generic for proper type safety\n- Create proper interfaces for API responses and state types\n- Use `Record<string, unknown>` for flexible object types\n- Add type guards for standardized error responses\n\nFiles changed:\n- websocket.service.ts: Use proper type casting for message data\n- mobile-swipe.component.ts: Make SwipeEvent and component generic\n- smart-preloading.strategy.ts: Type Navigator connection API properly\n- progress-feedback.service.ts: Use Record<string, unknown> for details\n- logger.service.ts: Replace any with Record<string, unknown>\n- error-handling.service.ts: Use unknown with type guards\n- privacy-api.service.ts: Create typed interfaces for API responses\n- error-correlation.service.ts: Use instanceof Error checks\n- detailed-results.component.ts: Type error handling properly\n- keyboard-navigation.service.ts: Type window extensions\n- i18n.service.ts: Use unknown for translation traversal\n- pwa.service.ts: Type sync data and IndexedDB properly\n- campaign.component.ts: Type custom event handlers\n- create-job.component.ts: Type job completion handlers\n- jobs-list.component.ts: Create proper state interfaces\n- mobile-results-item.component.ts: Use generic SwipeEvent type\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [CLEAN-006] Fix TypeScript warnings (TS7053, TS6138)\n\n- Fixed ExperienceMetrics interface to match actual return type from calculateExperience()\n  - Added seniorityLevel: string\n  - Changed completenessScore to confidenceScore\n- Fixed TS2345 by providing fallback value for optional fileName parameter\n- Removed unused @ts-expect-error directive (TS2578) in global-teardown.ts\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [SPLIT-001] Split incentive.dto.ts into modular files\n\nSplit the 1,182-line incentive.dto.ts into 7 modular files under 500 lines each:\n- incentive-enums.ts (60 lines) - All enums\n- incentive-interfaces.ts (73 lines) - All interfaces\n- incentive-value-objects.ts (463 lines) - Value objects\n- incentive-results.ts (131 lines) - Result classes\n- incentive-events.ts (180 lines) - Domain events\n- incentive-aggregate.ts (443 lines) - Incentive aggregate root\n- index.ts (54 lines) - Barrel export for backward compatibility\n\nOriginal incentive.dto.ts now re-exports from the modular directory.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [SPLIT-002] Split jobs.service.ts using facade pattern\n\nSplit jobs.service.ts (1,084 lines) into modular files under 500 lines:\n- jobs.service.ts (461 lines): Main facade that delegates to sub-services\n- jobs-semantic-cache.service.ts (280 lines): Semantic cache operations\n- jobs-event.service.ts (391 lines): NATS subscriptions and event handlers\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [SPLIT-003] Split parsing.service.ts using orchestrator pattern\n\n- Split parsing.service.ts (1,086 lines) into 5 modular files under 500 lines\n- Created parsing-event.service.ts (233 lines): NATS event publishing\n- Created parsing-retry.service.ts (313 lines): Error handling and retry logic\n- Created parsing-health.service.ts (119 lines): Health checks and metrics\n- Created parsing-file.service.ts (178 lines): File operations and validation\n- Refactored parsing.service.ts (246 lines): Main orchestrator facade\n- Created barrel export index.ts for sub-services\n- Maintained backward compatibility with existing tests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: Update progress log for SPLIT-003\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [SPLIT-004] Split scoring-confidence.service.ts using facade pattern\n\n- Split scoring-confidence.service.ts (1,013 lines) into 5 modular files\n- Created confidence/ subdirectory with:\n  - confidence.types.ts (161 lines): All interfaces for confidence metrics\n  - data-quality.service.ts (264 lines): Data quality assessment\n  - analysis-reliability.service.ts (154 lines): Analysis reliability assessment\n  - confidence-report.service.ts (355 lines): Score variance, recommendations\n  - index.ts (27 lines): Barrel export\n- Refactored main service (214 lines) as facade delegating to sub-services\n- Updated spec file to test sub-services directly\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(batch1): complete TEST-001 TEST-002 and clean ts unused diagnostics\n\n* feat: [CLEAN-007] Remove unused imports and commented-out code blocks\n\n- Removed \"reserved for future use\" commented imports from frontend components\n- Removed commented-out passport imports from auth guards and strategies\n- Cleaned up commented mock implementations in services\n- Converted dead code to TODO comments where functionality is pending\n- Preserved architectural comments explaining ESM compatibility decisions\n\nAll tests pass (3093 tests), lint passes (27 projects), typecheck passes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [SPLIT-007] Split infrastructure-shared index.ts into modular exports\n\nSplit the 1,090-line index.ts into 9 modular directories:\n- common/enums.ts (76 lines): All enums\n- common/interfaces.ts (49 lines): Base interfaces\n- filters/exception-filter.ts (63 lines): Exception filter classes\n- interceptors/interceptor-types.ts (100 lines): Interceptor types\n- validation/input-validator.ts (68 lines): Input validator\n- encryption/encryption.ts (71 lines): Encryption service\n- contracts/design-by-contract.ts (303 lines): DBC decorators\n- resilience/retry.ts (80 lines): Retry utility\n- resilience/circuit-breaker.ts (39 lines): Circuit breaker\n- errors/domain-exceptions.ts (62 lines): Domain exceptions\n- errors/error-correlation.ts (33 lines): Error correlation\n- monitoring/database-monitor.ts (77 lines): DB performance monitor\n\nMain index.ts now a pure barrel export (93 lines).\nAll files under 500 lines. Backward compatibility maintained.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [SPLIT-005, SPLIT-006A] Split usage-limit.controller.ts and experience-calculator.spec.ts\n\nSPLIT-005: Verified usage-limit.controller.ts was already split into sub-controllers\n- usage-limit-quota.controller.ts (271 lines)\n- usage-limit-admin.controller.ts (361 lines)\n- usage-limit-analytics.controller.ts (270 lines)\n\nSPLIT-006A: Split experience-calculator.spec.ts (2,577 lines) into basic tests file\n- experience-calculator-basic.spec.ts (473 lines): Single position, multiple positions,\n  empty input, month/year conversion tests\n- experience-calculator.spec.ts: Retained overlap detection, gap detection, and\n  seniority level determination tests\n\nAll 125 tests pass across both spec files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [SPLIT-006B] - Split experience-calculator.spec.ts edge cases\n\nSplit the remaining 2,093-line experience-calculator.spec.ts into 4 modular files:\n- experience-calculator-overlap.spec.ts (248 lines): Overlap detection tests\n- experience-calculator-gap.spec.ts (462 lines): Gap detection tests\n- experience-calculator-seniority-entry-mid.spec.ts (99 lines): Entry/Mid level tests\n- experience-calculator-seniority-senior-expert.spec.ts (168 lines): Senior/Expert level tests\n\nAll 85 tests pass across 5 test suites. All files are under 500 lines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [SPLIT-008] - Split report.repository.ts\n\nSplit report.repository.ts (964 lines) into 3 modular files:\n- report.types.ts (193 lines): All interfaces, types, and allowed sort fields\n- report-analytics.repository.ts (417 lines): Analytics operations (getReportAnalytics, getJobAnalytics, getTimeSeriesAnalytics)\n- report.repository.ts (480 lines): Core CRUD operations delegating to analytics repository\n\nAll files now under 500 lines. Backward compatibility maintained through re-exports.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [SPLIT-009] - Split validation.util.ts into domain-specific validators\n\n- Split validation.util.ts (979 lines) into 7 modular files\n- Created validators directory with:\n  - validation.types.ts (85 lines): All interfaces\n  - email.validator.ts (178 lines): EmailValidator class\n  - phone.validator.ts (189 lines): PhoneValidator class\n  - id.validator.ts (156 lines): IdValidator class\n  - schema.validator.ts (251 lines): SchemaValidator class\n  - validator.ts (176 lines): Generic Validator class\n  - index.ts (24 lines): Barrel export\n- Refactored validation.util.ts as barrel export\n- Fixed unused import in usage-limit-admin.controller.ts\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [SPLIT-010] - Verify analytics.controller.ts already meets size requirements\n\nVerified analytics.controller.ts is 114 lines (well under 500 line limit).\nOriginal PRD line count of 902 was incorrect or file was previously refactored.\nNo splitting required - file is already optimal size.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [STUB-001A] - Configure Gemini API client in app-gateway\n\n- Added GEMINI_API_KEY to appGateway environment schema (optional)\n- Configured GeminiClient provider in CommonModule with SecureConfigValidator\n- Provider gracefully handles missing API keys (returns undefined if not set)\n- Follows same pattern as scoring-engine-svc for fail-fast security\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [STUB-001B][STUB-002] - Implement real Gemini API calls for JD extraction\n\n- Add GeminiClient integration to jd-extractor-svc LlmService\n- Implement extractWithGemini() for AI-powered job description parsing\n- Preserve keyword-based extraction as fallback when Gemini unavailable\n- Add proper dependency injection with @Optional() decorator\n- Configure GeminiClient provider in app.module.ts using JdExtractorConfigService\n- Add comprehensive test coverage for Gemini API integration and fallback scenarios\n- Higher confidence scores (0.85) with Gemini vs fallback (0.65)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: [SPLIT-005] Add missing controller files for usage-limit split\n\n- Add usage-limit.types.ts with type definitions\n- Add usage-limit-analytics.controller.ts\n- Add usage-limit-quota.controller.ts\n- Add controllers/index.ts barrel export\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: [CodeQL] Fix security vulnerabilities in input-validator.ts\n\n- Fix incomplete multi-character sanitization (line 205)\n  - Now properly removes <script> tags and encodes < and > characters\n- Fix bad HTML filtering regexp (line 503)\n  - Updated regex to handle whitespace in closing tags (e.g., </script >)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: [CodeQL] Improve HTML sanitization security\n\n- Use entity encoding approach for HTML validation (more robust)\n- Escape &, <, >, \", and '' characters to prevent injection\n- Fix regex patterns to handle all whitespace types in closing tags\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jackela <jackela@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9e94939a56af4108318bb70b28b015bb71d0b7fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jackela/AI-Recruitment-Clerk/git/trees/9e94939a56af4108318bb70b28b015bb71d0b7fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jackela/AI-Recruitment-Clerk/git/commits/40a1b8845bd73535038fcedc405ef5d328822e33","verification":{"payload":"tree 9e94939a56af4108318bb70b28b015bb71d0b7fc\nparent ec25258209c21e09921aefb0f998d6fd4e2f6ea1\nauthor Jackela <k740724287@gmail.com> 1772080397 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1772080397 +0800\n\nrefactor: [CLEAN-001] Replace `any` types in 8 shared-dtos files (#47)\n\n* refactor: [CLEAN-001] Replace `any` types in 8 shared-dtos files\n\nPartial progress on CLEAN-001 - fixing `any` type usages in shared-dtos library.\n\nChanges:\n- Replace `Record<string, any>` with `Record<string, unknown>`\n- Replace `data: any` in restore methods with typed interfaces\n- Replace `...args: any[]` with `...args: unknown[]` in decorators\n- Replace `event: any` with `DomainEvent` or `unknown` with type guards\n\nFiles fixed:\n- contracts/analytics.contracts.ts\n- domains/analytics.rules.ts\n- domains/incentive.dto.ts\n- domains/incentive.rules.ts\n- domains/usage-limit.service.ts\n- domains/user-management.dto.ts\n- encryption/encryption.service.ts\n- infrastructure/redis/redis.client.ts\n\nRemaining: 19 files still have `any` usages\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: Fix broken links, standardize versions, add env validation to microservices\n\n- Fix README.md documentation links to point to existing files\n- Update Node.js version requirement from 18+ to 20.18.0+ (matches CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- Fix Angular version badge in Chinese README from 18 to 20\n- Standardize DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md to use npm instead of pnpm\n- Add validateEnv() to all 4 microservices for fail-fast startup:\n  - resume-parser-svc\n  - jd-extractor-svc\n  - scoring-engine-svc\n  - report-generator-svc\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [CLEAN-001] Verify and complete shared-dtos any type removal\n\nVerified CLEAN-001 acceptance criteria are met:\n- No @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any errors in shared-dtos source files\n- npm run lint for shared-dtos passes (0 errors, 21 warnings for different rules)\n- npm test passes (819 tests)\n\nThe previous commit (8d1e061) already fixed most any types. Remaining any\nusages are only in test files (.spec.ts, .test.ts) which are acceptable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [CLEAN-002] Fix any types in app-gateway services\n\n- Create analytics.dto.ts with proper typed DTOs\n- Reorder ReportFiltersDto before GenerateReportDto to fix circular dependency\n- Fix test to provide required DTO properties (metricName, value)\n- All lint checks pass with 0 any type errors\n- All 398 tests pass\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [CLEAN-003] Fix any types in resume-parser-svc\n\n- Created internal types file (parsing.types.ts) with proper type definitions\n- Updated ResumeSubmittedEvent with organizationId and fileMetadata fields\n- Replaced all `any` types in source files with proper typed interfaces:\n  - ResumeSubmittedEventData, ResumeParseSuccessResult, RetryOriginalData\n  - HealthCheckDetails, ResumeStatusUpdateData, SkillsQueryFilter, SortOption\n  - ExperienceMetrics, SecuredResumeDto\n- Fixed type compatibility issues with Mongoose Sort and Record<string, unknown>\n- All 432 tests pass, lint passes with 0 errors\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [CLEAN-004] Fix any types in scoring-engine-svc\n\n- Created internal interfaces for Gemini API response types:\n  - SemanticMatchResponse for skill matching\n  - SkillImprovementSuggestion and ImprovementSuggestionsResponse\n- Used generic type parameter with generateStructuredResponse<T>()\n- All 183 tests pass, lint passes with 0 errors\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [CLEAN-005] Fix any types in frontend\n\n- Replace all `any` types with proper TypeScript types in frontend source files\n- Use `unknown` with type guards for error handling\n- Make SwipeEvent generic for proper type safety\n- Create proper interfaces for API responses and state types\n- Use `Record<string, unknown>` for flexible object types\n- Add type guards for standardized error responses\n\nFiles changed:\n- websocket.service.ts: Use proper type casting for message data\n- mobile-swipe.component.ts: Make SwipeEvent and component generic\n- smart-preloading.strategy.ts: Type Navigator connection API properly\n- progress-feedback.service.ts: Use Record<string, unknown> for details\n- logger.service.ts: Replace any with Record<string, unknown>\n- error-handling.service.ts: Use unknown with type guards\n- privacy-api.service.ts: Create typed interfaces for API responses\n- error-correlation.service.ts: Use instanceof Error checks\n- detailed-results.component.ts: Type error handling properly\n- keyboard-navigation.service.ts: Type window extensions\n- i18n.service.ts: Use unknown for translation traversal\n- pwa.service.ts: Type sync data and IndexedDB properly\n- campaign.component.ts: Type custom event handlers\n- create-job.component.ts: Type job completion handlers\n- jobs-list.component.ts: Create proper state interfaces\n- mobile-results-item.component.ts: Use generic SwipeEvent type\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [CLEAN-006] Fix TypeScript warnings (TS7053, TS6138)\n\n- Fixed ExperienceMetrics interface to match actual return type from calculateExperience()\n  - Added seniorityLevel: string\n  - Changed completenessScore to confidenceScore\n- Fixed TS2345 by providing fallback value for optional fileName parameter\n- Removed unused @ts-expect-error directive (TS2578) in global-teardown.ts\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [SPLIT-001] Split incentive.dto.ts into modular files\n\nSplit the 1,182-line incentive.dto.ts into 7 modular files under 500 lines each:\n- incentive-enums.ts (60 lines) - All enums\n- incentive-interfaces.ts (73 lines) - All interfaces\n- incentive-value-objects.ts (463 lines) - Value objects\n- incentive-results.ts (131 lines) - Result classes\n- incentive-events.ts (180 lines) - Domain events\n- incentive-aggregate.ts (443 lines) - Incentive aggregate root\n- index.ts (54 lines) - Barrel export for backward compatibility\n\nOriginal incentive.dto.ts now re-exports from the modular directory.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [SPLIT-002] Split jobs.service.ts using facade pattern\n\nSplit jobs.service.ts (1,084 lines) into modular files under 500 lines:\n- jobs.service.ts (461 lines): Main facade that delegates to sub-services\n- jobs-semantic-cache.service.ts (280 lines): Semantic cache operations\n- jobs-event.service.ts (391 lines): NATS subscriptions and event handlers\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [SPLIT-003] Split parsing.service.ts using orchestrator pattern\n\n- Split parsing.service.ts (1,086 lines) into 5 modular files under 500 lines\n- Created parsing-event.service.ts (233 lines): NATS event publishing\n- Created parsing-retry.service.ts (313 lines): Error handling and retry logic\n- Created parsing-health.service.ts (119 lines): Health checks and metrics\n- Created parsing-file.service.ts (178 lines): File operations and validation\n- Refactored parsing.service.ts (246 lines): Main orchestrator facade\n- Created barrel export index.ts for sub-services\n- Maintained backward compatibility with existing tests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: Update progress log for SPLIT-003\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [SPLIT-004] Split scoring-confidence.service.ts using facade pattern\n\n- Split scoring-confidence.service.ts (1,013 lines) into 5 modular files\n- Created confidence/ subdirectory with:\n  - confidence.types.ts (161 lines): All interfaces for confidence metrics\n  - data-quality.service.ts (264 lines): Data quality assessment\n  - analysis-reliability.service.ts (154 lines): Analysis reliability assessment\n  - confidence-report.service.ts (355 lines): Score variance, recommendations\n  - index.ts (27 lines): Barrel export\n- Refactored main service (214 lines) as facade delegating to sub-services\n- Updated spec file to test sub-services directly\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(batch1): complete TEST-001 TEST-002 and clean ts unused diagnostics\n\n* feat: [CLEAN-007] Remove unused imports and commented-out code blocks\n\n- Removed \"reserved for future use\" commented imports from frontend components\n- Removed commented-out passport imports from auth guards and strategies\n- Cleaned up commented mock implementations in services\n- Converted dead code to TODO comments where functionality is pending\n- Preserved architectural comments explaining ESM compatibility decisions\n\nAll tests pass (3093 tests), lint passes (27 projects), typecheck passes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [SPLIT-007] Split infrastructure-shared index.ts into modular exports\n\nSplit the 1,090-line index.ts into 9 modular directories:\n- common/enums.ts (76 lines): All enums\n- common/interfaces.ts (49 lines): Base interfaces\n- filters/exception-filter.ts (63 lines): Exception filter classes\n- interceptors/interceptor-types.ts (100 lines): Interceptor types\n- validation/input-validator.ts (68 lines): Input validator\n- encryption/encryption.ts (71 lines): Encryption service\n- contracts/design-by-contract.ts (303 lines): DBC decorators\n- resilience/retry.ts (80 lines): Retry utility\n- resilience/circuit-breaker.ts (39 lines): Circuit breaker\n- errors/domain-exceptions.ts (62 lines): Domain exceptions\n- errors/error-correlation.ts (33 lines): Error correlation\n- monitoring/database-monitor.ts (77 lines): DB performance monitor\n\nMain index.ts now a pure barrel export (93 lines).\nAll files under 500 lines. Backward compatibility maintained.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [SPLIT-005, SPLIT-006A] Split usage-limit.controller.ts and experience-calculator.spec.ts\n\nSPLIT-005: Verified usage-limit.controller.ts was already split into sub-controllers\n- usage-limit-quota.controller.ts (271 lines)\n- usage-limit-admin.controller.ts (361 lines)\n- usage-limit-analytics.controller.ts (270 lines)\n\nSPLIT-006A: Split experience-calculator.spec.ts (2,577 lines) into basic tests file\n- experience-calculator-basic.spec.ts (473 lines): Single position, multiple positions,\n  empty input, month/year conversion tests\n- experience-calculator.spec.ts: Retained overlap detection, gap detection, and\n  seniority level determination tests\n\nAll 125 tests pass across both spec files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [SPLIT-006B] - Split experience-calculator.spec.ts edge cases\n\nSplit the remaining 2,093-line experience-calculator.spec.ts into 4 modular files:\n- experience-calculator-overlap.spec.ts (248 lines): Overlap detection tests\n- experience-calculator-gap.spec.ts (462 lines): Gap detection tests\n- experience-calculator-seniority-entry-mid.spec.ts (99 lines): Entry/Mid level tests\n- experience-calculator-seniority-senior-expert.spec.ts (168 lines): Senior/Expert level tests\n\nAll 85 tests pass across 5 test suites. All files are under 500 lines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [SPLIT-008] - Split report.repository.ts\n\nSplit report.repository.ts (964 lines) into 3 modular files:\n- report.types.ts (193 lines): All interfaces, types, and allowed sort fields\n- report-analytics.repository.ts (417 lines): Analytics operations (getReportAnalytics, getJobAnalytics, getTimeSeriesAnalytics)\n- report.repository.ts (480 lines): Core CRUD operations delegating to analytics repository\n\nAll files now under 500 lines. Backward compatibility maintained through re-exports.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [SPLIT-009] - Split validation.util.ts into domain-specific validators\n\n- Split validation.util.ts (979 lines) into 7 modular files\n- Created validators directory with:\n  - validation.types.ts (85 lines): All interfaces\n  - email.validator.ts (178 lines): EmailValidator class\n  - phone.validator.ts (189 lines): PhoneValidator class\n  - id.validator.ts (156 lines): IdValidator class\n  - schema.validator.ts (251 lines): SchemaValidator class\n  - validator.ts (176 lines): Generic Validator class\n  - index.ts (24 lines): Barrel export\n- Refactored validation.util.ts as barrel export\n- Fixed unused import in usage-limit-admin.controller.ts\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [SPLIT-010] - Verify analytics.controller.ts already meets size requirements\n\nVerified analytics.controller.ts is 114 lines (well under 500 line limit).\nOriginal PRD line count of 902 was incorrect or file was previously refactored.\nNo splitting required - file is already optimal size.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [STUB-001A] - Configure Gemini API client in app-gateway\n\n- Added GEMINI_API_KEY to appGateway environment schema (optional)\n- Configured GeminiClient provider in CommonModule with SecureConfigValidator\n- Provider gracefully handles missing API keys (returns undefined if not set)\n- Follows same pattern as scoring-engine-svc for fail-fast security\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: [STUB-001B][STUB-002] - Implement real Gemini API calls for JD extraction\n\n- Add GeminiClient integration to jd-extractor-svc LlmService\n- Implement extractWithGemini() for AI-powered job description parsing\n- Preserve keyword-based extraction as fallback when Gemini unavailable\n- Add proper dependency injection with @Optional() decorator\n- Configure GeminiClient provider in app.module.ts using JdExtractorConfigService\n- Add comprehensive test coverage for Gemini API integration and fallback scenarios\n- Higher confidence scores (0.85) with Gemini vs fallback (0.65)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: [SPLIT-005] Add missing controller files for usage-limit split\n\n- Add usage-limit.types.ts with type definitions\n- Add usage-limit-analytics.controller.ts\n- Add usage-limit-quota.controller.ts\n- Add controllers/index.ts barrel export\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: [CodeQL] Fix security vulnerabilities in input-validator.ts\n\n- Fix incomplete multi-character sanitization (line 205)\n  - Now properly removes <script> tags and encodes < and > characters\n- Fix bad HTML filtering regexp (line 503)\n  - Updated regex to handle whitespace in closing tags (e.g., </script >)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: [CodeQL] Improve HTML sanitization security\n\n- Use entity encoding approach for HTML validation (more robust)\n- Escape &, <, >, \", and '' characters to prevent injection\n- Fix regex patterns to handle all whitespace types in closing tags\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jackela <jackela@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpn80NCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA43